BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261116T190000Z
DTEND:20261116T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20261117T040040Z
UID:6ljrmos4ts93jabs41nh2evmr1@google.com
CREATED:20261104T164758Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>The Department of Chemical and Systems Biology Presents a Sp
 ecial Seminar &amp\; Open Discussion<br></b><br><b>David Garfield\, PhD</b>
 <br><i>AI for Life Sciences\, Partnerships\, Anthropic</i><br><br><b>Monday
 \, November 16\, 2026</b><br>11:00 AM – 12:45 PM<br>Munzer Auditorium<br><b
 r><b>Discussion Moderators:</b> Joanna Wysocka &amp\; Jordan Valgardson  <b
 r><b><br></b><br><b>Talk Title: </b>“Science with Claude: agentic biology\,
  data analysis\, and human interactions in a world of LLMs”<br><br><b>An op
 en discussion with the speaker will immediately follow the seminar presenta
 tion.</b> Attendees are encouraged to bring their questions\, perspectives\
 , and ideas for an engaging conversation.<br><br><b>Abstract:</b> Large lan
 guage models are now good enough at reading\, coding and reasoning to take 
 on real pieces of a research project\, and that changes what a day at the b
 ench or the keyboard looks like. In this talk I'll show how scientists are 
 using Claude and Claude Science as agentic collaborators. The worked exampl
 es come from my own field of regulatory genomics: interpreting non-coding g
 enetic variants with sequence-to-function models\, and designing enhancers 
 and promoters with defined activity. I'll cover what works\, where agents s
 till mislead\, and which habits keep the science rigorous. I'll close with 
 how Anthropic is working with academic labs. An open discussion follows\, s
 o please bring questions\, skeptical ones included.<br><br><b>Speaker Bio:<
 /b> David Garfield works on AI for Life Sciences partnerships at Anthropic\
 , where he builds research collaborations with universities and research in
 stitutes. He trained as an evolutionary developmental biologist and quantit
 ative geneticist\, did his postdoc with Eileen Furlong at EMBL\, and then l
 ed an ERC-funded research group at Humboldt University in Berlin. He moved 
 to industry at Bayer and then Genentech\, where he was a Principal Scientis
 t in computational biology working on human genetics\, regulatory genomics 
 and machine-learning models of sequence function. He joined Anthropic in 20
 26.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T180644Z
LOCATION:Munzer Auditorium 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CSB Special Seminar & Open Discussion: David Garfield\, PhD
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
